extraction_notes: "WB17 Warlords of Russia printed 78-79 (cache p079-p080, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer. The general Reaver O.C.C.s material that applies to all five Reaver classes runs printed 76-77 (cache p077 line 95 to p078); this class''s own heading The Average Reaver Soldier and its stat block start on cache p079 and the entry ends with Money and Cybernetics on p080. || HEADING: the stat block is headed Typical Reaver Grunt/Warrior O.C.C. and NPC Villain, also known as Raiders and Peasent Warriors (the book''s spelling); it is a playable O.C.C., listed under Warlord Troops and Men at Arms O.C.C.s on printed 57, so men_of_arms is true and occ_group is men-of-arms. || XP: the ladder shared with the Russian Explorer and Reaver Military Scout on the Experience Tables, printed 6, read off a render. The book misprints level 7 as 30,501; level 6 ends at 31,500, so 31501 is stored. || SKILLS: Speaks Native Language at 90% stored as base 90. The O.C.C. skill Piloting: two of choice (+5%) prints no exclusion and is stored as any Pilot. Related Pilot Skills are printed Any, except robots, ships and aircraft; that is read as the catalog rows Robots and Power Armor, Robot Combat: Basic, Robot Combat Elite and its eleven per-robot rows, Boat: Ships, Military: Warships and Patrol Boats, Airplane, Jet Aircraft, Helicopter, Military: Combat Helicopter and Military: Jet Fighters. Science Math only is read as both Mathematics rows. Mechanical is printed Basic Mechanics and Automotive only. || MONEY: 1D6x100 credits stored (the text layer prints !D6xlOO); the 5D6x10 credits of tradeable goods (printed 5D6xlO) and the 500 credit monthly salary are in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: one weapon for each W.P.; folding shovel, bedroll, belt, boots and a handful of personal items have no row. The armor choice offers this book''s two homemade armor rows; the modern armor alternative is in the note. Tinted goggles, the lighter and the language translator use the nearest catalog rows and say so in their notes. || AS PRINTED: the Equipment Available On Assignment line says the Scout may have access to special weapons, explosives, equipment, vehicles and troops, in the soldier''s entry; it is in GM Notes as this class''s. || NOT STORED: the background lines of the general Reaver section (25-35% of a Warlord''s forces, 1-3% D-Bees, 20-33% with a few implants or one or two bionic limbs) and its statement that characters with magic or psionics or other foreign O.C.C.s may be Reavers but use their own O.C.C."
